;; Payments-Core Demo — Beat C: two-account conservation (PAIR-RET).
;;
;; The visceral "money cannot be created or destroyed" property wants a post over
;; BOTH balances at once: the two account balances after a transfer sum to the two
;; balances before. Before PAIR-RET this was inexpressible — `first`/`second` were
;; not in the predicate sort env, so a pair-return post fell back to `asserted`.
;;
;; `conserve` returns the (from', to') pair and proves the conservation sum directly:
;;
;;   (first result) + (second result)  =  from + to
;;
;; reached at the body-faithful (verified) tier — the pair is constructed in the body
;; and the projections discharge through z3's datatype theory (the single-constructor
;; product restriction of the COMP-4 datatype class). The refuted twin
;; (conserve-bad.llmll) credits one extra unit — money creation — and is refuted.
;;
;;   llmll verify ./conserve.llmll --trust-report   ->  conserve verified

(def conserve [from: int to: int amount: int] -> (int, int)
  (pre  (and (>= from amount) (>= amount 0)))
  (post (= (+ (first result) (second result)) (+ from to)))
  (pair (- from amount) (+ to amount)))
